<project xmlns="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:schemaLocation="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0 http://maven.apache.org/xsd/maven-4.0.0.xsd">
    <modelVersion>4.0.0</modelVersion>

	<parent>
		<groupId>org.gjs</groupId>
		<artifactId>gjs</artifactId>
		<version>1.0.0-RC.1</version>
		<relativePath>..</relativePath>
	</parent>
	
    <artifactId>gjs-parent</artifactId>
	<packaging>pom</packaging>

    <name>GJS Parent</name>    
    <description>
	Common parent pom for all kind of projects and archetypes.
	
	Profiles:
		* win-base              : It is automatically selected based on the operating system is Windows
		* win | unix | cygwin   : It is automatically selected based on the operating system
								  cygwin is activated if the operating system is Windows and the CYGWIN environment variable has been defined.
		* linux 	            : It is automatically selected based on the operating system. If is selected unix profile is also active.
	
		* debug		            : It is activated if the DEBUG porperty has been defined

		* pom | source 			: It is automatically selected when the project has packaging pom or not 
		* plugin 				: It is automatically selected when the project has packaging maven-plugin 

		* eclipse               : It is automatically selected when Maven is executed from Eclipse IDE
	
	Special properties;
	
		* skip.if.not.source    :  true if packaging is pom, false otherwise
	
	Environtment propeties:
	
		* CYGWIN: To activate cygwin profile instead the windows profile 
					export CYGWIN=1
				  To deactivate cygwin profile 		
					export CYGWIN
		.
		To compile on pure Windows (without Cygwin) the gcc and g++ compiler executables need to be accessible
		in the PATH. 
					
	Needs properties in settings.xml file: 
		
		* cygwinDir : Directory of Cygwin installation (indirectly, only for cygwin profile)

		* cygwinUser : Username for Cygwin (indirectly, only for cygwin profile)
					
	</description>    

